## Composed messages: resolved in RUST at event time with Fluent arguments,
## delivered to the chrome in the event payload, rendered verbatim -- the
## same pattern describe_off already uses. Runtime values cross as args and
## are never concatenated into FTL. The rule clause is its own message so
## its inclusion stays a Rust decision, not a translation decision; the
## {" "} literal carries the joining space FTL would otherwise trim.

chrome-blocked-body = PATANYX did not open { $host } because it has been reported for phishing or malware.{ $rulenote } If you believe this is wrong, you can open it anyway. That applies to this tab only and ends when you close it.
chrome-adlist-body = PATANYX did not open { $host } because it is on the ad and tracker list. That list is built for the requests pages make in the background, so a site you typed yourself can end up on it. You can open it anyway; that applies to { $host } in this tab only and ends when you leave it or close the tab. Nothing else on the list is unblocked.
chrome-adlist-body-post = PATANYX did not open { $host } because it is on the ad and tracker list. Your form was not sent, and Open anyway will not send it: it loads the address without what you typed. That applies to { $host } in this tab only and ends when you leave it or close the tab. Nothing else on the list is unblocked.
chrome-adlist-body-no-exception = PATANYX did not open { $host } because it is on the ad and tracker list. That list is built for the requests pages make in the background, so a site you typed yourself can end up on it. On Linux there is no way to open a single site past the list. You can turn blocking off in the Privacy panel, which turns it off for every site until you turn it back on.
chrome-adlist-exception-button = Ad list exception
chrome-adlist-exception-title = PATANYX is letting this tab reach this host past ad and tracker blocking. Ends when you leave it or close the tab.
chrome-blocked-rule-clause = {" "}It matched the rule { $rule }, which also covers its subdomains.

