chrome-dnsp-resolver-description-p = Encrypted does not mean unseen. Quad9 sees every site you look up.
chrome-dnsp-resolver-description-p-n2 = The site name is encrypted when the site supports it, but the IP address of the server you connect to remains visible. If the lookup itself is unencrypted, your network can interfere with it and strip away the information needed to enable that protection.
chrome-dnsp-resolver-description-p-n3 = Quad9 never falls back to network DNS, because a fallback would hand your lookups to the network in the open. That breaks public WiFi sign-in. On hotel or airport WiFi, switch to System, restart, and sign in.
