chrome-keep-sites-caption-p = PATANYX clears cookies and site data every time it starts. A site listed here is left alone, so it still knows you next time. Useful for a site that signs you out or re-verifies you on every launch.
chrome-keep-sites-h3 = Sites to keep when PATANYX starts
chrome-keep-sites-limit-p = Keeping any site changes how the clear works. Instead of wiping the whole profile at once, PATANYX clears each site it can find in the cookie jar. A site that stored data but set no cookie is not found that way, so its data can survive. With no sites kept, the whole profile is cleared as before.
chrome-devtools-caption-p = Opens the inspector for the page you are looking at, the same as Ctrl+Shift+I. Here as a button as well, because a keyboard shortcut has to reach the right window and a button does not.
chrome-devtools-choice-h3 = Developer tools
chrome-devtools-open-button = Open developer tools
chrome-tracking-prevention-balanced-button = Balanced
chrome-tracking-prevention-caption-p = Strict blocks the most and can break some sites, including Google apps. Balanced is WebView2's default and rarely breaks anything. PATANYX's own blocker works the same under both.
chrome-tracking-prevention-choice-h3 = Engine tracker blocking
chrome-tracking-prevention-scope-p = Windows only. A change reaches the WebView2 profiles behind tabs open now and tabs opened later. PATANYX does not reload a page; reload it to give the next navigation the new level from its first request.
chrome-tracking-prevention-strict-button = Strict
