chrome-dns-compare-quad9-rest = Swiss nonprofit. Encrypted. Blocks only malware and phishing, so it rarely breaks a page. States it validates signed answers (DNSSEC) and sends none of your IP address to queried servers. Sees every domain you look up, and never falls back to network DNS, so public WiFi sign-in needs System.
chrome-dns-compare-system-rest = Uses an active VPN's resolver; otherwise your internet provider's. This browser leaves lookups unencrypted, letting a provider log what you look up and, in some places, sell it. Blocks nothing, and supports public WiFi sign-in.
chrome-premium-activation-lead = On a network that blocks EdgeXene, activate without a connection. On your phone, or any device that can get online, open
chrome-premium-activation-rest = and enter this device's ID together with your Premium token. Paste the code it gives you below. The code only works on this computer, so it is safe to carry across on a phone screen.
chrome-bk-import-warning-lead = Importing
chrome-bk-import-warning-rest = . Every password, note, and bookmark here is replaced by the backup. There is no undo. Export anything the backup does not contain first.
